Third-party material in this tree:
- kit/*/files/: whole engine files of 1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM and vllm-project/vllm (Apache-2.0) with this build's changes.
  The files keep that project's licence and headers. The engine they apply to is the engine of PLI Labs' eight-card
  builds (1Cat-vLLM #1277 with the patch series of Volta sPLIt and the native expert path of Volta Max uPLIft). One
  file, models/deepseek_v41/card_limit.py, is new and is ours. Comment lines that named a private working repository
  were reworded in the published copies; each MANIFEST says so.
- tools/tm_dispatch_emulation.py: a Python re-implementation of the dispatch cost model of the TurboMind GEMM
  (lmdeploy, "Copyright (c) OpenMMLab"), as carried in the engine's csrc/sm70_turbomind/lmdeploy/ tree. No TurboMind
  source is copied into this repository.
- The routed experts are served through 1Cat-vLLM's sm70_skinny QPN MoE backend (#742), whose kernels come from
  dnv2003/v100-skinny (MIT; LICENSES/MIT-v100-skinny.txt); no v100-skinny source is copied here.
- tests/data/: single log lines of this build's own boots, of one boot of the eight-card build and of the
  conversation store's CPU runs, used as test fixtures. They hold no prompt and no generated text.

No model weights, packs, wheels, compiled libraries, routing tallies, tier maps or prompt corpora are distributed
here. DeepSeek supplies the model, its MXFP4 experts, the DSpark drafter and the Engram design (MIT); NVIDIA the
NVFP4 pack (MIT); ISTA-DASLab the GSQ-RCO GGUF quantization (MIT). See CREDITS.md for every project this work
builds on.
